•2071-2100 (longo-prazo).

The 10-Year Integrated Solid Waste Management Plan (ISWMP) of Butuan City is anchored on the provisions of Republic Act No. 9003, otherwise known as the Ecological Solid Waste Management Act of 2000. Its primary objective is to establish an integrated waste-to-energy facility to ensure maximum waste diversion and, in the long term, prevent the costly construction and operation of a Sanitary Landfill Facility (SLF).

To effectively address current issues and challenges, the plan outlines the following key strategies:

- Intensify information, education, and communication (IEC) campaigns and trainings for all solid waste management stakeholders;

- Enforce strictly all existing SWM laws, policies, ordinances, and related issuances;

- Strengthen monitoring and evaluation of barangay compliance with RA 9003, while providing incentives and awards for best practices;

- Expand waste collection services to achieve full coverage;

- Convert the SLF into a sorting, recycling, and processing plant;

- Deploy sufficient and well-equipped SWM enforcers; and

- Ensure adequate budget allocation for the procurement of SWM equipment and facilities.
